are always terminated after the niter variable inside the newton method reaches two. Of
course, this is no real surprise because a function of this nature is an ideal case for the
Newton algorithm. The same would occur for any other convex quadratic function; i.e.,
the newton method for class Optim would always return the exact (to machine precision)
minimizer with niter = 2 (Exercise 8.14).
